WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.670
At Site 19, many anomalies are kept secure.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:06.180
One, however, does not fit in with the rest.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:11.900
He is a caucasian man of around fifty-five
years of age, who at first glance seems normal

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:12.969
in every way.

00:00:12.969 --> 00:00:17.640
He’s average height, average weight, and
dressed in business attire.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:23.810
Calling himself Gustav Nobel, he seems to
be a perfectly pleasant American man who seems

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:28.590
deeply out of place compared to the hundreds
of other objects and entities kept at the

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.050
largest SCP containment facility.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.590
So why is he so closely guarded?

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:37.480
What secrets are kept inside this man’s
head?

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:44.120
To understand why SCP-657 is so important,
one has to go back to his recovery.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:49.510
Mr. Nobel worked for years as an undertaker
at a funeral home in the United States, not

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:50.810
raising any attention.

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:55.690
But there was a man who worked for him, and
they didn’t get along.

00:00:55.690 --> 00:01:02.000
They argued frequently, and one day SCP-657
had to correct the man’s work, something

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.150
that he had to do frequently.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:07.210
They argued, and suddenly Mr. Nobel got angry.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.920
He yelled out “What does it matter?

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.840
You’ll be dead before the end of the week!”.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:17.100
There were multiple people present, and they
all thought Mr. Nobel must be losing his mind.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.200
That is, until it came true.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:25.250
Three days later, the man was working on his
home when he slipped and fell from his roof.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:29.990
He was killed instantly, in what would seem
like a tragic accident.

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:34.250
There was no evidence pointing to another
cause of death, but many people remembered

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:39.909
Mr. Nobel’s outburst at work and reported
him to the authorities as a possible killer.

00:01:39.909 --> 00:01:44.119
That was enough for the police, and they arrested
Mr. Nobel.

00:01:44.119 --> 00:01:48.850
They were never able to find any physical
evidence linking him to the case, but they

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:51.460
questioned him relentlessly.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:56.830
While he never indicated that he was responsible,
Mr. Nobel did make similar comments about

00:01:56.830 --> 00:02:01.020
one of the arresting officers also being close
to death.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:07.360
That man met his own end two days later, when
a suspect fatally shot him during an apprehension.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:13.159
The two deaths seemed unrelated, but the police
didn’t believe it - and neither did the

00:02:13.159 --> 00:02:14.609
SCP Foundation.

00:02:14.609 --> 00:02:18.790
The police were convinced that this normal
looking man had somehow been involved in the

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:24.180
officer’s death, and they made a request
for federal assistance as they investigated.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:28.780
While they didn’t understand what had happened,
they knew they wanted to see the man pay for

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.129
his crimes.

00:02:30.129 --> 00:02:35.659
The justice system moved quickly, and Gustav
Nobel was put on trial for both murders.

00:02:35.659 --> 00:02:40.889
In near-record time, he was convicted of one
murder and of conspiracy to commit the other,

00:02:40.889 --> 00:02:43.329
and he was sentenced to death.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:47.739
According to the officers who apprehended
him, he would soon be facing the death chamber

00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:50.120
and justice would be done.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.480
But it was all a lie.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.849
The SCP Foundation is quite experienced with
extracting prisoners.

00:02:56.849 --> 00:03:01.709
Condemned prisoners are one of their best
sources for the recruiting of D-Class Personnel,

00:03:01.709 --> 00:03:05.699
and they know how to remove a prisoner from
incarceration and leave the authorities no

00:03:05.699 --> 00:03:07.989
clue that anything went awry.

00:03:07.989 --> 00:03:12.269
They used those procedures to retrieve Mr.
Nobel before his date with the executioner

00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:18.169
- but unlike most inmates the Foundation plucks
death row, this one wasn’t headed for D-Class

00:03:18.169 --> 00:03:19.169
duty.

00:03:19.169 --> 00:03:22.760
The Foundation believed he was much more important
than that.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:29.879
They knew that this man, who would soon be
classified as SCP-657, had a unique link to

00:03:29.879 --> 00:03:31.519
death itself.

00:03:31.519 --> 00:03:38.590
Once secured at Site 19, SCP-657 was debriefed
and investigated by Foundation officials,

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:42.230
which is when they became aware of the full
extent of his abilities.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:48.889
SCP-657 has the ability to predict the time
of anyone’s death - sometimes with terrifying

00:03:48.889 --> 00:03:49.959
accuracy.

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:54.629
All it takes for him to make a prediction
is for him to make physical contact with the

00:03:54.629 --> 00:03:58.790
person, which can be something as simple as
shaking their hand.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:03.970
The prediction is involuntary - as soon as
he makes contact, he gets the information

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.670
about how much longer they have to live.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:11.689
He was able to predict the deaths of the two
men he made contact with down to the day - but

00:04:11.689 --> 00:04:16.239
when exposed to some D-Class Personnel who
had already been slated for termination the

00:04:16.239 --> 00:04:20.600
next day, he was able to make predictions
down to the minute.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:26.060
But there’s one weak spot in SCP-657’s
predictions.

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:31.040
The closer the person he makes contact with
is to their moment of death, the more accurate

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.260
he is.

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:34.540
But that works in reverse as well.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.940
If he touches someone who is still far away
from their time of death, his predictions

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.220
get fuzzier.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:45.290
He can still predict the general time of death,
but if it’s a decade or more away, all he

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:48.600
can see is the year with no more details.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:54.500
No matter how accurate the time he gives is,
he never gets any other information - such

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.290
as the cause of death.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:59.340
All he gets is a number inside his head.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:04.600
But while the details might be unclear, they
are no less accurate, and every prediction

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:11.470
SCP-657 has made about the time of death has
been proven true.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:16.370
SCP-657’s powers seem to work the same on
every living person, although there are a

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.150
few odd exceptions.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:23.340
When tested on a select few SCP Agents and
Doctors, he claimed that his abilities came

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.340
up empty.

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:28.970
He simply couldn’t see a time of death for
them, and investigations and testing proved

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:30.970
he was telling the truth.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:38.169
This indicates that future investigations
about these flukes should center not on SCP-657

00:05:38.169 --> 00:05:40.950
- but on the individuals who seem to be immune.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:46.810
So far, though, no common link or explanation
has been found between them other than the

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:49.810
fact that they all work for the Foundation.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:55.490
What does stay consistent is the reaction
people have to SCP-657.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:06:00.190
When encountering him, people will nearly
always report that they find him strange,

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:01.720
unpleasant, or “Creepy”.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:06.290
They may be sensing his abilities, even if
they’re not aware of them.

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:10.640
But when they’re informed that he can predict
the time of death, the unsettling feeling

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.090
seems to escalate.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:17.620
When they don’t know, they simply can’t
identify what causes them to have this disturbing

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:18.620
feeling.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:25.240
Could this be a milder but similar effect
to that caused by SCP-053, a small child who

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:28.540
makes otherwise stable people feel compelled
to act violently?

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:35.480
Right now, the reaction people have to SCP-657
is not considered a source of concern, but

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:38.830
the foundation is keeping an eye on it.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:45.580
SCP-657 is an unusual specimen in other ways
too though, and that requires unusual protocols.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:51.810
SCP-657 is one of the lowest-security residents
at Site 19, with his living quarters being

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:56.960
a large room with a queen-sized bed and any
reasonable amenities he requests.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:02.060
He’s not considered a threat to escape and
displays no hostility, so the main concern

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:05.590
is keeping him healthy and stable for future
testing.

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:10.370
His nutritional needs are taken care of, with
the staff providing him with daily meals and

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:14.080
vitamins, along with medication for his arthritis.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:19.390
His quarters look closer to a hotel room than
to a cell, and initially he was able to move

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:25.110
around Site 19 as he wished as long as he
was accompanied by a staff member of proper

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.110
security.

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:28.080
So why did this have to change?

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:33.990
Nothing differed in SCP-657’s behavior and
no attempts to escape or security breaches

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:34.990
were made.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:41.290
However, what did become clear was that SCP-657
freely wandering around the facility was a

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:47.330
danger - not to others, but to himself if
he encountered the wrong being.

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:54.610
This stems from an experiment where SCP-657
was introduced to SCP-076, better known as

00:07:54.610 --> 00:08:00.800
“Able” and he is one of the most volatile
SCPs in Site 19.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:07.150
SCP-076 consists of two separate entities,
a black cube of engraved stone, and the humanlike,

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:10.750
heavily tattooed male figure that resides
inside it.

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:15.590
While Able spends most of his time dormant
in a deathlike state, he occasionally awakens

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:21.080
and seeks out the nearest human being - which
he then seeks to kill unless he himself is

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.280
terminated.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:26.310
When killed, he eventually reincarnates within
the cube.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:33.449
SCP-076 is a puzzle to the foundation - and
they thought SCP-657 could help them answer

00:08:33.449 --> 00:08:34.449
it.

00:08:34.449 --> 00:08:41.800
SCP-657 was introduced to SCP-076-2, as the
humanoid Able is officially designated, under

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:47.399
pretenses of having him join Mobile Task Force
Omega-7 - an experimental team consisting

00:08:47.399 --> 00:08:51.100
of some powerful but controllable SCPs.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:59.449
This was really a way to see if SCP-657 could
answer any questions about SCP-076-2’s lifespan.

00:08:59.449 --> 00:09:04.291
Given the being’s supernatural nature and
unique resurrection process, it’s not a

00:09:04.291 --> 00:09:07.740
huge surprise that the answer… was no.

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:11.540
What was a surprise was how SCP-657 reacted.

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:19.749
The process of determining someone’s lifespan
is usually quick and easy for SCP-657.

00:09:19.749 --> 00:09:23.499
The numbers will usually appear in his mind
in just seconds.

00:09:23.499 --> 00:09:29.000
But when he touched SCP-076-2, things went
very wrong.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.769
His eyes immediately rolled back into his
head and he collapsed.

00:09:32.769 --> 00:09:37.370
There was no physical cause for this, but
he fell into a coma and didn’t wake up for

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:38.629
over a week.

00:09:38.629 --> 00:09:43.120
After he woke up, he was examined for any
lingering health issues and interviewed so

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:46.100
the Foundation could learn what he experienced.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.249
It turns out the answer was that he experienced…
nothing.

00:09:49.249 --> 00:09:56.649
He had no memory of the events, or of even
meeting SCP-076-2 at all.

00:09:56.649 --> 00:10:02.180
This indicates that either SCP-657’s abilities
won’t work on anything that’s not technically

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:09.360
human - or that SCP-076-2 simply doesn’t
have a lifespan and will continue to reincarnate

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:10.360
forever.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:14.769
It was clear that SCP-657 had an Achilles’
heel.

00:10:14.769 --> 00:10:20.879
Exposure to humanlike but ultimately inhuman
SCPs had the potential to mess with his abilities

00:10:20.879 --> 00:10:23.910
and create serious adverse side effects.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:28.399
While this time he had recovered in only a
week, no one knew if the next time would cause

00:10:28.399 --> 00:10:29.560
lasting damage.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:33.889
It was determined that security measures needed
to be increased.

00:10:33.889 --> 00:10:39.069
SCP-657 would be confined to his quarters,
with two security staff members stationed

00:10:39.069 --> 00:10:41.730
outside his door at all times.

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:48.449
As SCP-657 has no unusual or dangerous physical
abilities, security is still minimal compared

00:10:48.449 --> 00:10:53.850
to other SCPs, and the foundation has instructed
the site to grant all reasonable requests

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:58.790
for entertainment and furnishments to ensure
his mental health stays stable.

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:03.709
But there is one other thing the foundation
is still trying to avoid.

00:11:03.709 --> 00:11:09.740
The staff has been ordered to keep their distance
from SCP-657 and avoid physical contact unless

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:11.889
absolutely necessary.

00:11:11.889 --> 00:11:18.060
This is because accidental contact, giving
SCP-657 access to the death information, could

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:20.540
be stressful for both parties.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:26.759
The knowledge of someone’s pending death
has been shown to weigh on SCP-657, as seen

00:11:26.759 --> 00:11:32.670
in his initial outburst against his employee,
and not everyone wants to know how much time

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.189
they have left.

00:11:34.189 --> 00:11:41.399
Minimal physical contact is the best way to
preserve SCP-657’s use to the SCP Foundation.

00:11:41.399 --> 00:11:44.459
So what are the long-term plans for SCP-657?

00:11:44.459 --> 00:11:48.689
There are still many unanswered questions
about his ability.

00:11:48.689 --> 00:11:54.399
While he has now been prohibited from interacting
with other non-human SCPs for his own safety,

00:11:54.399 --> 00:11:59.649
he could still be used by the Foundation to
learn vital information about Foundation agents

00:11:59.649 --> 00:12:03.059
and the danger posed to them on upcoming missions.

00:12:03.059 --> 00:12:07.839
One question is - can the death date be altered
with advanced knowledge?

00:12:07.839 --> 00:12:11.970
For instance, could an agent who is slated
to die in two days on a mission be switched

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:14.559
off that mission to change their death date?

00:12:14.559 --> 00:12:19.720
Or would this create a time paradox, potentially
upsetting our reality by trying to change

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:20.720
it.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:25.120
These and many other experiments will likely
be tried by the Foundation in the future,

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:29.370
once a safe method for testing them is developed
and approved.

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:34.579
The research continues though, since the best
chance the SCP Foundation has at answering

00:12:34.579 --> 00:12:41.110
the great mysteries of death may just rest
in the unassuming older man in Site 19.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:47.319
For more on another unassuming older man with
unique abilities, check out “SCP-662 - Butler’s

00:12:47.319 --> 00:12:52.399
Hand Bell”, or watch “SCP-053 - Young
Girl” for more on that strange case.

